  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=470 head=ab9e275b605b99316d0a2525f7d219a6d794f0e5 -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 470 @ ab9e275b605b\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=n/a)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-09T04:07:37Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-461-weighted-line-collision` onto `main`; merge base `a111c34ab3ca8b0db115b73156ddcd5bf886e9f8`; head `ab9e275b605b99316d0a2525f7d219a6d794f0e5`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/ConsistencyPositivity.lean:45` \u2014 Reuse the shared placement calculus instead of introducing duplicate positivity, summation, and commutation proofs.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/SubLinePrefix.lean:11` \u2014 The module description reverses which coordinate blocks vanish under prefix truncation.  <!-- lane=code -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\n**F1: Duplicated placement infrastructure.** `reindexOp_nonneg`, `place_finset_sum_local`, and the two local commutation proofs duplicate declarations added in `Points/Placement.lean` at lines 90, 138, and 218. This creates parallel implementations of the same register calculus.\n\nImport and reuse that API, or place it in a shared lower-level module. In particular, I verified that `place_mul_place_nonneg` follows directly from the existing placement lemmas and Mathlib\u2019s `Commute.mul_nonneg` (`Mathlib/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/ContinuousFunctionalCalculus/Instances.lean:292`):\n```lean\nexact Commute.mul_nonneg (S.place_nonneg p\u2081 hX) (S.place_nonneg p\u2082 hY)\n  (S.place_comm p\u2081 p\u2082 hopp X Y)\n```\nThis removes the need for the duplicated case-specific infrastructure. Requires changes under the modularity criterion.\n\n**F2: Incorrect mathematical description.** Prefix truncation makes preceding blocks vanish and leaves later blocks unchanged, not conversely. The source specifies that the projection \u201czeroes out the first \\(i-1\\) coordinates\u201d: `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:237`, following `eq:cl-dlnf`; blueprint `def:ld-question-distribution` repeats this at `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:58`. The actual lemmas `projX_directPrefixProjection_embZ` and `projZ_directPrefixProjection_embX` are correct. Fix the reversed module description.\n\n**Statement Integrity.** The completed point construction preserves the hypotheses, measurement spaces, quantifier order, and consistency conclusions of `lem:qld-4-10`, with a universal error `K \u03b5^(1/8)`. The restricted-average results retain the source\u2019s `2m` and `4m\u00b2` factors. No new load-bearing bridge assumptions were found. The directly indexed sub-line construction and nondegenerate collision estimate remain explicitly scoped auxiliaries.\n\n**Verification.** `Points.lean`, `Lines.lean`, `WeightedCollision.lean`, and `ConsistencyPositivity.lean` type-check. Axiom checks for the five main completed results report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. No new proof holes or forbidden bypasses were found.\n\nResidual work remains in the two unchanged joint-line construction `sorry` sites, zero-direction collision handling, and transport to the source extended-line carrier. I did not rerun the full build. The checkout is unchanged.\n",
